# Schematics and graphical assets

The supplied folder contains several figures that can be classified as framework schematics rather than numerical-result plots.

## Primary framework schematics

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `K.png` | Integrated forward–inverse–optimization workflow for geometry-driven WAAM control. This is the **primary architecture schematic**. |
| `K4.png` | Comparison between conventional open-loop deposition and the proposed geometry-driven two-layer WAAM refinement framework. |
| `K2.png` | Two-layer WAAM deposition/refinement illustration showing the proposed geometry-driven workflow. |
| `K5.png` | Two-layer WAAM deposition illustration with process/geometry comparison. |
| `C.png` | Layer-2 / forward–inverse–optimization framework schematic. |
| `B.png` | Two-layer WAAM workflow/validation schematic. |
| `A.png` | Two-layer WAAM workflow variant. |

## Result figures

The remaining PNG files are primarily model-performance or optimization-result figures, including:

- `A11.png`, `A12.png` — AISI 316 forward-model results;
- `L1.png` — ER70S-6 forward-model results;
- `C1.png`–`C5.png`, `CC2.png`–`CC4.png` — inverse-model parameter predictions;
- `C6.png`, `C7.png`, `D1.png` — optimization convergence;
- `C8.png` — optimized process parameters;
- `AS1.png`–`AS4.png`, `E1.png`, `E2.png`, `G1.png`, `SL1.png` — additional forward-model/result plots.

## Recommended repository presentation

For a public repository, the primary README should display `K.png` as the conceptual overview, followed by `K4.png` as the experimental/two-layer validation schematic. Numerical performance plots should be grouped separately under `figures/results/`.

The original PNG files are retained without modification so that the repository remains traceable to the manuscript source package.
